{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HEB",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore leaving the principles of the doctrine of Christ, let us go on to perfection; not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith towards God,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of the doctrine of baptisms, and of laying on of hands, and of the resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And this will we do, if God permit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " impossible for those who have been once enlightened, and have tasted the heavenly gift, and have been made partakers of the Holy Spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And have tasted the good word of God, and the powers of the world to come,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If they shall fall away, to renew them again to repentance; seeing they crucify to themselves the Son of God afresh, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to an open shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the earth which drinketh in the rain that cometh often upon it, and bringeth forth herbs fit for them by whom it is dressed, receiveth blessing from God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But that which beareth thorns and briers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rejected, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nigh to cursing; whose end ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be burned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But, beloved, we are persuaded better things of you, and things that accompany salvation, though we thus speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not unrighteous to forget your work and labor of love, which ye have shown towards his name, in that ye have ministered to the saints, and do minister.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And we desire every one of you to show the same diligence to the full assurance of hope to the end:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That ye be not slothful, but followers of them who through faith and patience inherit the promises.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when God made promise to Abraham, because he could swear by no greater, he swore by himself,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, Surely blessing I will bless thee, and multiplying I will multiply thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And so, after he had patiently endured, he obtained the promise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For men verily swear by the greater: and an oath for confirmation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to them an end of all contradiction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherein God, willing more abundantly to show to the heirs of promise the immutability of his counsel, confirmed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by an oath:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That by two immutable things, in which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " impossible for God to lie, we might have a strong consolation, who have fled for refuge to lay hold upon the hope set before us:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hope",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " we have as an anchor of the soul, both sure and steadfast, and which entereth into that within the vail;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whither the forerunner hath for us entered, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jesus, made a high priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
